{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>Fuzzy matching and virtualized lists both have keyboard implications</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      Fuzzy matching (so "gh iss" finds "GitHub Issues") is a search-quality feature, but it also has a keyboard-UX side: the highlighted/first result should reset to the top of the list on every keystroke, or a user who types fast can hit Enter on a stale selection from a previous filter pass.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      If the result list is long enough to virtualize (rendering only visible rows), the highlighted-item tracking has to work against the full filtered dataset, not just the currently-rendered DOM slice — arrow-key-down past the last rendered row needs to scroll the list and keep the highlight in sync, not just stop moving because the next item isn't mounted yet.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      Verify the whole interaction with a screen reader on, not just visually: <code>aria-activedescendant</code> announcements should read the highlighted option's label as it changes, the palette needs <code>role="dialog"</code> with <code>aria-modal="true"</code> (or equivalent) so background content is excluded from the accessibility tree while open, and the trigger button needs <code>aria-expanded</code> kept in sync with actual open state — a command palette that "looks" keyboard-first in DevTools but wasn't checked with assistive tech reliably has at least one of these missing.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

