{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A search box that filters on type isn't a command palette until arrow keys, Enter, and Escape all work without ever touching the mouse.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Track the highlighted result via <code>aria-activedescendant</code> instead of moving real DOM focus per keystroke, and trap Tab/Shift+Tab inside the palette while it's open.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">Every exit path — Escape, click-outside, selecting a result, a route change — has to restore focus to the trigger the same way, or the happy path becomes the one case that loses it.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
